  "copper_scope": "Delete exactly two old gate segments and one R1406 OUT approach, identified by source hash and exact UUID/net/layer/endpoints/width snapshots. Add 12 segments, no vias. All other retained copper objects unchanged. Seven pads and five component-owned guard shapes follow the explicit poses; all native guard IDs, layers and prohibitions retained.",
  "electrical": "Q1401 drain and four dump resistor lands form one group. 0.48-mm corridor reaches all four resistors; source GND has a 0.48-mm corridor to the retained ground stitch. Old pad connections, 50 power-width checks, 155 GND pads, 63 critical adjacency and retained reference copper pass regression.",
  "opposite_face_projection_review": [
    {
      "reference": "L701",
      "nets": [
        "Net-(Q1401-G)"
      ],
      "review": "A short part of the B-side gate approach projects beneath the F-side inductor footprint. In4 reference is continuous under the full new stroke outside own pad lands; no new via is added, and the F buck/SW/feedback copper is unchanged. This is a documented coupling-sensitive candidate area; continuous ground does not prove immunity to magnetic coupling or gate glitches."
    },
    {
      "reference": "L901",
      "nets": [
        "Net-(Q1401-D)"
      ],
      "review": "B-side local traces project beneath parts of the F inductor footprint. In4 ground is retained beneath the full strokes; the drain route stays on B and has no new transfer. Switching-current coupling and inductor/dump-stage thermal interaction remain required whole-board/bench checks."
    }
  ],
  "thermal": "Q1401 moves 0.70 mm left and rotates toward existing dump resistors. No power dissipation or duty rating is upgraded. MOSFET pulse SOA, comparator loaded-gate timing, resistor duty/temperature, copper current capability and interactions with nearby buck inductors remain unqualified.",
